<p>Follow these steps to change the name and comment of a one click preset.</p>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">Manage...</span> on 
 the <span class="Term-Soft">Frequently Used Settings</span> tab. The <span class="Term-Soft">Manage One Click Preset List</span> dialog box appears.</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start="3">
<li><p>Select the one click preset name which you want 
 to change in <span class="Term-Soft">One Click Preset List:</span>.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">You cannot 
 change the name and comment of the system-provided one click preset.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="4">
<li><p>Change the one click preset name and comment in 
 the boxes below.<br/>
 The name can be up to 128 single-byte or 64 double-byte characters.<br/>
 The comment can be up to 512 single-byte or 256 double-byte characters. 
 You can insert line breaks.<br/>
 Make sure the name and comment have been changed in the list.</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start="5">
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to save 
 the changes and close the <span class="Term-Soft">Manage One Click Preset 
 List</span> dialog box.</p></li>
</ol>
